{"id":"mahabharata-5-146","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":146,"title":"षट्चत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 146 · Drona's and Vidura's words","summary":{"en":"Krishna continues: Drona told Duryodhana that the kingdom rightfully belongs to the Pandavas, and Vidura appealed to Bhishma, grieving that the Kuru race was being destroyed by Duryodhana's folly. Gandhari too rebuked her son and urged that Yudhishthira rule the inherited kingdom.","kn":"ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಮುಂದುವರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ: ರಾಜ್ಯ ನ್ಯಾಯವಾಗಿ ಪಾಂಡವರಿಗೆ ಸೇರಿದ್ದು ಎಂದು ದ್ರೋಣರು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳಿದರು; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಮೂರ್ಖತನದಿಂದ ಕುರುವಂಶ ನಾಶವಾಗುತ್ತಿದೆ ಎಂದು ವಿದುರನು ಭೀಷ್ಮನಿಗೆ ಮೊರೆಯಿಟ್ಟನು. ಗಾಂಧಾರಿಯೂ ಮಗನನ್ನು ಗದರಿಸಿ ಪಿತ್ರಾರ್ಜಿತ ರಾಜ್ಯವನ್ನು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಆಳಲಿ ಎಂದಳು.","hi":"श्रीकृष्ण आगे बताते हैं: द्रोण ने दुर्योधन से कहा कि राज्य न्यायतः पाण्डवों का है, और विदुर ने भीष्म से विनती की, शोक करते हुए कि दुर्योधन की मूर्खता से कुरुवंश नष्ट हो रहा है। गान्धारी ने भी पुत्र को फटकारा और आग्रह किया कि युधिष्ठिर पैतृक राज्य पर शासन करें।","te":"శ్రీకృష్ణుడు కొనసాగిస్తాడు: రాజ్యం న్యాయంగా పాండవులదేనని ద్రోణుడు దుర్యోధనునికి చెప్పాడు; దుర్యోధనుని మూర్ఖత్వం వల్ల కురువంశం నశిస్తోందని దుఃఖిస్తూ విదురుడు భీష్ముని వేడుకున్నాడు. గాంధారి కూడా కుమారుని మందలించి పిత్రార్జిత రాజ్యాన్ని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు పాలించాలని కోరింది.","ta":"ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் தொடர்கிறார்: அரசு முறைப்படி பாண்டவர்களுக்கே உரியது என்று த்ரோணர் துரியோதனனிடம் சொன்னார்; துரியோதனனின் மடமையால் குரு குலம் அழிகிறது என்று வருந்தி விதுரர் பீஷ்மரிடம் முறையிட்டார். காந்தாரியும் மகனைக் கடிந்து, மரபுவழி அரசை யுதிஷ்டிரர் ஆள வேண்டும் என்று வற்புறுத்தினாள்.","ml":"കൃഷ്ണൻ തുടരുന്നു: രാജ്യം പാണ്ഡവർക്ക് ന്യായമായി അവകാശപ്പെട്ടതാണെന്ന് ദ്രോണർ ദുര്യോധനനോട് പറഞ്ഞു; ദുര്യോധനന്റെ വിഡ്ഢിത്തത്താൽ കുരുവംശം നശിക്കുന്നതിൽ ദുഃഖിച്ച് വിദുരർ ഭീഷ്മരോട് അപേക്ഷിച്ചു. ഗാന്ധാരിയും മകനെ ശാസിച്ച്, അനന്തരാവകാശമായ രാജ്യം യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ഭരിക്കണമെന്ന് ആവശ്യപ്പെട്ടു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.146; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"कर्णोपनिवादपर्व","titleEn":"Karnopanivada Parva (The secret talks with Karna)","verses":[{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भीष्मेणोक्ते ततो द्रोणो दुर्योधनमभाषत ।\nमध्ये नृपाणां भद्रं ते वचनं वचनक्षमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhishma had spoken, Drona, skilled in speech, said to Duryodhana among the kings: \"May good come to you.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रातीपः शंतनुस्तात कुलस्यार्थे यथोत्थितः ।\nतथा देवव्रतो भीष्मः कुलस्यार्थे स्थितोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My child, as Shantanu, son of Pratipa, arose for the sake of the family, so Devavrata Bhishma has stood firm for the sake of the family."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः पाण्डुर्नरपतिः सत्यसंधो जितेन्द्रियः ।\nराजा कुरूणां धर्मात्मा सुव्रतः सुसमाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Pandu, the king, true to his word, master of his senses, righteous king of the Kurus, of good vows and concentrated mind,"}},{"n":4,"text":"ज्येष्ठाय राज्यमददाद्धृतराष्ट्राय धीमते ।\nयवीयसस्तथा क्षत्तुः कुरुवंशविवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"gave the kingdom to the elder, wise Dhritarashtra, and to the younger one, Vidura, the increaser of the Kuru line."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः सिंहासने राजन्स्थापयित्वैनमच्युतम् ।\nवनं जगाम कौरव्यो भार्याभ्यां सहितोऽनघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, my king, having seated that unfailing Dhritarashtra on the lion throne, the Kaurava, faultless, went to the forest with his two wives."}},{"n":6,"text":"नीचैः स्थित्वा तु विदुर उपास्ते स्म विनीतवत् ।\nप्रेष्यवत्पुरुषव्याघ्रो वालव्यजनमुत्क्षिपन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vidura stood below and attended humbly like a servant, that tiger among men raising the yak-tail fan."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः सर्वाः प्रजास्तात धृतराष्ट्रं जनेश्वरम् ।\nअन्वपद्यन्त विधिवद्यथा पाण्डुं नराधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the people, my dear, served Dhritarashtra, lord of men, rightly, as they had served King Pandu."}},{"n":8,"text":"विसृज्य धृतराष्ट्राय राज्यं स विदुराय च ।\nचचार पृथिवीं पाण्डुः सर्वां परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having handed over the kingdom to Dhritarashtra and Vidura, Pandu, conqueror of enemy cities, roamed the whole earth."}},{"n":9,"text":"कोशसंजनने दाने भृत्यानां चान्ववेक्षणे ।\nभरणे चैव सर्वस्य विदुरः सत्यसंगरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In gathering the treasury, in giving, in watching over the servants, and in the support of everyone, Vidura, true to his word, took charge."}},{"n":10,"text":"संधिविग्रहसंयुक्तो राज्ञः संवाहनक्रियाः ।\nअवैक्षत महातेजा भीष्मः परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty Bhishma, conqueror of enemy cities, saw to the king's services, peace and war."}},{"n":11,"text":"सिंहासनस्थो नृपतिर्धृतराष्ट्रो महाबलः ।\nअन्वास्यमानः सततं विदुरेण महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty King Dhritarashtra sat on the throne, always attended by great-souled Vidura."}},{"n":12,"text":"कथं तस्य कुले जातः कुलभेदं व्यवस्यसि ।\nसंभूय भ्रातृभिः सार्धं भुङ्क्ष्व भोगाञ्जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"How, born in that family, can you resolve to split it? Unite with your brothers and enjoy your pleasures, lord of the people."}},{"n":13,"text":"ब्रवीम्यहं न कार्पण्यान्नार्थहेतोः कथंचन ।\nभीष्मेण दत्तमश्नामि न त्वया राजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I say this not from poverty nor in any way for gain. I eat what Bhishma has given, best of kings, not what you give."}},{"n":14,"text":"नाहं त्वत्तोऽभिकाङ्क्षिष्ये वृत्त्युपायं जनाधिप ।\nयतो भीष्मस्ततो द्रोणो यद्भीष्मस्त्वाह तत्कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will not seek a living from you, lord of the people. Where Bhishma is, there is Drona; do what Bhishma says."}},{"n":15,"text":"दीयतां पाण्डुपुत्रेभ्यो राज्यार्धमरिकर्शन ।\nसममाचार्यकं तात तव तेषां च मे सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give half the kingdom to the sons of Pandu, scorcher of foes. My teaching is the same, my son, for you and for them."}},{"n":16,"text":"अश्वत्थामा यथा मह्यं तथा श्वेतहयो मम ।\nबहुना किं प्रलापेन यतो धर्मस्ततो जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthama is to me as the white-horsed Arjuna is. What use is much talk? Where there is dharma, there is victory.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"एवमुक्ते महाराज द्रोणेनामिततेजसा ।\nव्याजहार ततो वाक्यं विदुरः सत्यसंगरः ।\nपितुर्वदनमन्वीक्ष्य परिवृत्य च धर्मवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When immeasurably brilliant Drona had spoken thus, Vidura, true to his word and knower of dharma, then spoke, looking at his father's face and turning around."}},{"n":18,"text":"देवव्रत निबोधेदं वचनं मम भाषतः ।\nप्रनष्टः कौरवो वंशस्त्वयायं पुनरुद्धृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Devavrata, listen to what I say. The Kaurava line was lost, and you raised it up again."}},{"n":19,"text":"तन्मे विलपमानस्य वचनं समुपेक्षसे ।\nकोऽयं दुर्योधनो नाम कुलेऽस्मिन्कुलपांसनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet you pay no attention to my words as I lament. Who is this Duryodhana, this stain on the family,"}},{"n":20,"text":"यस्य लोभाभिभूतस्य मतिं समनुवर्तसे ।\nअनार्यस्याकृतज्ञस्य लोभोपहतचेतसः ।\nअतिक्रामति यः शास्त्रं पितुर्धर्मार्थदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"whose will you follow, overcome by greed as he is, ignoble, ungrateful, his mind struck down by greed, who transgresses the teaching of his father, who saw dharma and profit?"}},{"n":21,"text":"एते नश्यन्ति कुरवो दुर्योधनकृतेन वै ।\nयथा ते न प्रणश्येयुर्महाराज तथा कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"These Kurus are perishing because of what Duryodhana has done. Great king, act so that they do not perish."}},{"n":22,"text":"मां चैव धृतराष्ट्रं च पूर्वमेव महाद्युते ।\nचित्रकार इवालेख्यं कृत्वा मा स्म विनाशय ।\nप्रजापतिः प्रजाः सृष्ट्वा यथा संहरते तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lustrous one, do not destroy me and Dhritarashtra, long since drawn like figures in a painting by a painter, as Prajapati withdraws the creatures he has made."}},{"n":23,"text":"नोपेक्षस्व महाबाहो पश्यमानः कुलक्षयम् ।\nअथ तेऽद्य मतिर्नष्टा विनाशे प्रत्युपस्थिते ।\nवनं गच्छ मया सार्धं धृतराष्ट्रेण चैव ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed one, do not look on and ignore the destruction of the family. If your mind is lost now that destruction has come, go to the forest with me and Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":24,"text":"बद्ध्वा वा निकृतिप्रज्ञं धार्तराष्ट्रं सुदुर्मतिम् ।\nसाध्विदं राज्यमद्यास्तु पाण्डवैरभिरक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or else bind this ill-minded son of Dhritarashtra, of crooked wits, and let this kingdom be well guarded by the Pandavas today."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रसीद राजशार्दूल विनाशो दृश्यते महान् ।\nपाण्डवानां कुरूणां च राज्ञां चामिततेजसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be gracious, tiger among kings; great destruction is seen for the Pandavas, the Kurus, and the immeasurably mighty kings.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"विररामैवमुक्त्वा तु विदुरो दीनमानसः ।\nप्रध्यायमानः स तदा निःश्वसंश्च पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus, Vidura stopped, his mind dejected, brooding, and sighing again and again."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततोऽथ राज्ञः सुबलस्य पुत्री\nधर्मार्थयुक्तं कुलनाशभीता ।\nदुर्योधनं पापमतिं नृशंसं\nराज्ञां समक्षं सुतमाह कोपात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Gandhari, daughter of King Subala, afraid of the family's destruction, spoke angrily, in the presence of the kings, words full of dharma and profit to her son Duryodhana, who was evil-minded and cruel."}},{"n":28,"text":"ये पार्थिवा राजसभां प्रविष्टा\nब्रह्मर्षयो ये च सभासदोऽन्ये ।\nशृण्वन्तु वक्ष्यामि तवापराधं\nपापस्य सामात्यपरिच्छदस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let the kings who have entered the royal hall, the brahmin sages and the other members of the assembly, hear: I will tell of the offense of you, the sinner, with your ministers and retinue."}},{"n":29,"text":"राज्यं कुरूणामनुपूर्वभोग्यं\nक्रमागतो नः कुलधर्म एषः ।\nत्वं पापबुद्धेऽतिनृशंसकर्म-\nन्राज्यं कुरूणामनयाद्विहंसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kingdom of the Kurus is to be enjoyed in order of succession; this is our family's dharma, passed down. But you, evil-minded, of cruel deeds, destroy the Kuru kingdom by wrong."}},{"n":30,"text":"राज्ये स्थितो धृतराष्ट्रो मनीषी\nतस्यानुजो विदुरो दीर्घदर्शी ।\nएतावतिक्रम्य कथं नृपत्वं\nदुर्योधन प्रार्थयसेऽद्य मोहात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise Dhritarashtra is established in the kingdom, and his younger brother is far-seeing Vidura. Passing over these two, Duryodhana, how do you wish today, in delusion, for kingship?"}},{"n":31,"text":"राजा च क्षत्ता च महानुभावौ\nभीष्मे स्थिते परवन्तौ भवेताम् ।\nअयं तु धर्मज्ञतया महात्मा\nन राज्यकामो नृवरो नदीजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king and his minister, both of great power, are subordinate while Bhishma stands. But the Ganga's son, best of men, great-souled, out of his knowledge of dharma, has no desire for the kingdom."}},{"n":32,"text":"राज्यं तु पाण्डोरिदमप्रधृष्यं\nतस्याद्य पुत्राः प्रभवन्ति नान्ये ।\nराज्यं तदेतन्निखिलं पाण्डवानां\nपैतामहं पुत्रपौत्रानुगामि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This unassailable kingdom was Pandu's, and now only his sons have the right to it, no others. All this kingdom belongs to the Pandavas, their grandfather's inheritance, passing to sons and grandsons."}},{"n":33,"text":"यद्वै ब्रूते कुरुमुख्यो महात्मा\nदेवव्रतः सत्यसंधो मनीषी ।\nसर्वं तदस्माभिरहत्य धर्मं\nग्राह्यं स्वधर्मं परिपालयद्भिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever Devavrata says, the great-souled chief of the Kurus, true to his word and wise, we should accept it all, without violating dharma, keeping our own duty."}},{"n":34,"text":"अनुज्ञया चाथ महाव्रतस्य\nब्रूयान्नृपो यद्विदुरस्तथैव ।\nकार्यं भवेत्तत्सुहृद्भिर्नियुज्य\nधर्मं पुरस्कृत्य सुदीर्घकालम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the leave of the great-vowed one, let what the king and Vidura say be done by their friends, who engage in it for a very long time, putting dharma first."}},{"n":35,"text":"न्यायागतं राज्यमिदं कुरूणां\nयुधिष्ठिरः शास्तु वै धर्मपुत्रः ।\nप्रचोदितो धृतराष्ट्रेण राज्ञा\nपुरस्कृतः शांतनवेन चैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"This kingdom of the Kurus came by right; let Yudhishthira, the son of Dharma, rule it, urged by King Dhritarashtra and honored by Shantanu's son.\""}}]}]}